// expect-exit: 0
mod:assignment_target_runs_before_its_value_ok;
// AN ASSIGNMENT'S TARGET RUNS BEFORE ITS VALUE (DEF-571, landing 177d2b2): right programs that order lets stand, each beside its wrong twin in the rejection file.
// A jump in the value leaves with what the target did (`oe_asg_val_ix_p` against `oe_asg_ix_val_p`, `oe_cmp_val_ix_p` against `oe_cmp_ix_val_p`, `oh_field_tgt2_p` against `oh_field_tgt_p`), a jump in the target with nothing the value did
// (`og_asg_ix_val`, `oh_field_tgt_g`: restored), and a target may assign what the value reads (`oi15` against `oi1`). What the target does to itself before the value runs is no matter of this rule (`oi17`, `oi21`, `sb10`, `oi32`).
// A NAME STANDS STILL WHILE THE VALUE RUNS AND NO LONGER: not at a later statement (`hq8c`, `hq11`, `sb11`, `sb12`, `sb14`), and not if no target read it (`hq0`, `hq10`, `hsc2`, `sb13`, `oi35c`). A value's `defer` over other names is nothing to it (`hr5g`).
// A claim in the target isn't a read (`sa9`). A name read on another arm or in a loop's earlier trip isn't read unassigned (`oi30`, `oi31`).
// AN INLINE ARRAY OR STRUCT THAT CAN'T DROP IS THE PLACE ITSELF, so assigning one in the value leaves the address good (`ae1`, `ae3`, `ae7`, `gk4a`, `gk5`, `gk6`, `gk7`, `mc4`), and a field's or an element's write or claim is no event (`sa11`, `sb1`, `sb2`).
// A call in the target stands if the value leaves its name alone (`kc1`, `kc3`, `ok3`, `ok4`; `ok1` and `ok2` left at landing 177d2b3, where DEF-575 refuses them as its named prices: `tests/analysis/rejection/list_ptr_from_call.npk`), and a macro in the value is judged by what it expands to (`mc1c`, `mc2c`, `mc3c`).
error:Bad;
